  abstract = {In many fields of application, meta-analyses routinely involve dependent effect size estimates and hierarchical data structures. Statistical methods for analysing dependent effect sizes are now well-developed, but there has been less attention paid to the initial stages of data analysis, prior to formal modelling. We propose a generic workflow for preliminary, exploratory analyses of meta-analytic databases that involve dependent effect sizes, which focuses on validating the integrity of the input data and informing decisions about subsequent statistical modelling. The workflow entails creating summaries and visualizations of features of the primary studies included in the meta-analysis to aid in understanding the structure and distribution of the data, especially with respect to between- and within-study variation. We illustrate the workflow using data from previously published meta-analyses and discuss connections between the preliminary analysis and subsequent statistical modelling strategies.This article is part of the theme issue ‘Statistical workflow’.},
